Yay! After much toil and trouble, I present my first ascended character. :)

The character ended up become quite tough, and I could've probably
managed some conducts to boot, but I chose to play very safely since
this was my first to-be-Demigoddess. I was quite heavily spoiled, so it
may not be that amazing, but ascending is ascending. :)

Here follows her story (and what led to it), or at least what I remeber
of it. It's quite long, I'm somewhat exhilarated right now. :)

















Spoily, hence spoiler space.




















I recently had a promising rogue that had wished Grayswandir for himself
and was kicking fiendish butt with satisfactory performance. His
ascension was not to be, however, when a water demon appeared from a
fountain when he was trying to dilute potions. The water demon didn't
really put up a fight and teleported away. After I passed by it later,
it summoned Yeenoghu.

Panicking, I tried to flee using a wand of digging and after Yeenoghu
followed, a cursed scroll of teleportation. Yeenoghu started pounding on
me, but surprisingly did no significant damage, and I forced him to flee,
after which I fled. Later I encountered a cockatrice corpse, and
foolishly thought I could use it for some easy experience.  Gloves,
check. Full hp, check. Wield c corpse. "Surely he can't finish me off in
one round." Up the stairs... Yeenoghu hits, Yeenoghu hits, DYWYPI? 70
points in one round came as a surprise, as he did 10-20 on average
earlier. Well, die and learn...

After that I was a bit pissed off and started playing kamikaze
valkyries, Bjoerk being one of them. Bjoerk dived quickly to minetown,
where she encountered a magic lamp, which was promptly blessed. I had
some mithril gear from the mines and chose to go for a weapon, wishing
for Frosty. Sensing potential in Bjoerk, I started playing somewhat
cautiously.

Frosty did a fine job with the dungeon inhabitants. A momentary lapse
made me eat a little dog in Sokoban, and I lost my pet. Sokoban was BoH.
Mines' End was the mimic one (which I seem to get 90% of the time). Got
the luckstone and found an another BoH (and two more later).

An altar with at least two Hearse bones was found on dlvl 7, yielding at
least a magic marker. I put up a stash there and started sacrificing.
Didn't get anything useful from Odin though. After a while I started
descending. Found a throne room somewhere around dlvl 12-16. Third #sit
got me a wish, which was spent on +2 GDSM.

Alchemy got me enough !oGL for level 14 and I think I had AC -27 at that
point, so off for the Quest I went. The giants turned out to a bunch of
pansies. Bjoerk promptly killed, tinned and ate them until strength was
18/**. One of the giants had a wand of death which Bjoerk happily took
from him. Lord Surtur was astoundingly weak. Still, as he gulped down a
potion of invisibility and I had lost my potions of see invisibility to
fire traps, the battle quickly became very annoying with him teleporting
around. While chasing him off, I misstepped into lava, but a wand of
teleportation saved me. For punishment, Lord Surtur was subsequently
pummeled to death and tinned.

Identifying items was a real pain. I must've blessed and read and later
written, blessed and read something like 8-10 scrolls of identify,
getting exactly 0 full identifications. Of course, I had my inventory
full of unidentified stuff each and every time. Found an altar
somewhere, and burned wands of monster creation on it until Mjollnir was
obtained.

I had picked up a ring of levitation somewhere. Used it for crossing the
Medusa level and hacked Medusa to death. She was tinned as well. As I
didn't have reflection at that point, I was hoping for the shield off
Perseus, but no luck. Below Medusa were a couple of maze levels. On one
of them, a master mind flayer was detected using telepathy. Now, I had
read very, very nasty things about them. Also, I was only fast, and had
no grease. I chose to return up and ID my scrolls, hopefully finding
genocide among them.

After many turns spent ID-ing, no genocides were found. Did some more
alchemy and got HP up again. In frustration I #sat on the throne,
but it soon vanished. Went down to the mines again, hoping for a
genocide. No genocide was found in the mines, but RNG finally smiled on
me. A random monster dropped a pair of boots, which were identified as
speed boots, and an Aleax dropped a polished silver shield. I also
recalled the fancy word one can use for scaring monsters. As a
precaution against blinding, a blessed scroll of scare monster was also
used. The MMF went down gracefully, and I found myself in the castle.

Castle was a piece of cake. I carefully eliminated the nasty eels in the
pool, and then destroyed the drawbridge. Then I pushed a nearby boulder
in the moat and set up camp a knight's move away from the opening.
Monsters started pouring in. Three normal liches, but no other monsters
worth mentioning.

Castle wand had only one charge, but at least I had found a charging
scroll. Fearing brainlessness and summon nasties, the first wish was
spent on 2 blessed scrolls of genocide, to the dismay of all things L
and h. My ascension kit had started looking good (I also had found a
robe somewhere), but I thought I'd need a missile weapon, so I wished
for some gauntlets of power. After the first marker had dried, I wished
for a second one. Fooproofed and enchanted everything up to +4 and +5.

Didn't know what to wish for next, so I stashed my wand. After saving
the game at this point and loading it later, I found the throne looking
strangely attractive. First #sit got me uncomfortable, but the second
one got me an another wish! Yay! I didn't yet have a T-shirt, so I
wished for a blessed +2 fireproof one and gave a silly name to it. After
enchanting the shirt and doing some more alchemy, it was VotD for the
first time for me.

The RNG then chose to grant me more boons still. VotD had an insane
bones level containing at least two pairs of speed boots, SDSM, a wand
of death, Magicbane and the Eye of Aethiopica. Didn't really need the
armor, so I stashed it, but I greedily grabbed the other goodies.

Off to Gehennom it was. Asmodeus turned out to be very annoying,
teleporting in and out but fortunately doing no damage. My AC was around
-43 or something at this point. When I got to the up stairs and started
pummeling him, he levelported to someplace (I later found him 6 levels
up from there). Juiblex was easily dispatched using a wand of digging
and Frost Brand. Baalzebub was also very annoying with his stun attacks,
but a cockatrice appeared, tempting me with it's corpse. Baalzebub
didn't appreciate the corpse very much, but I sure appreciated smashing
his statue.

Vlad's tower was uneventful. Opted to wear "oLS just in case. Vlad was a
total pansy. Orcus-town was shortly reached. I was somewhat wary of him
summoning Demogorgon, which he didn't end up doing. He was hacked to
death with Frosty and Bjoerk pried the wand from his dead, cold fingers.

Afterwards I descended quickly using up a wand of digging. Marked the
vibrating square with a zorkmid and used the Eye and the Orb to teleport
to my stashes (located at dlvl 7 and the castle). I didn't want to fool
around with the Amulet, so I now did my final preparations. I got
crowned in order to avoid summary decapitation on Astral and stashed
Vorpy. I had chosen to use Mjollnir in Gehennom so I wouldn't destroy
potions, and sure enough I had a pile of them now. Did yet more alchemy
and made holy water. I also used up Gehennom gold for donations. AC was
now -46 and hit points were around 370.

While using the Eye to port to Vlad's to speed up descent, I found a
magic lamp there. It was cursed and I didn't feel like I'd need more
wishes, so I just carried it around. Found a huge pile of gold from the
zoo in the wizard's tower, so I ported back up once more to donate. AC
went down to -47 and I went back to the tower. The Eye started giving me
strange "I you feel disoriented for a moment." messages at this point.
Did it run out of charges or something?

Rodney Double Troubled as soon as I saw him, and I couldn't line them up
for a death ray, so I hacked them to little frozen bits instead. Got
the book and started wielding Magicbane to avoid malignant auras. Went
down and did the invocation. The sanctum yielded a couple of wraith
corpses and some monster also dropped a !oGL. The high priest went down
easily. Rodney appeared again near the stairs, but a wand of death made
short work of him.

The mysterious force left me alone for the longest time, but then
started being a major pain in the rear as I got closer to the surface. I
must have travelled the 37-33 area at least something like four or five
times. Rodney appared once along the way, but was death zapped.

Picked up my gems and ?oGD at my stashes and got to dlvl 1.
Double-checked that the amulet was real and off for the planes Bjoerk
went. Rodney was again dispatched with a wand of death. I used the Orb
of Weight to locate the magic portal and dug my way to it. The air plane
was somewhat more dangerous than what I had expected. Even with my armor
and the Orb, I think I took something like 70 damage there. A forgotten
spell provided confusion and the magic portals were found easily enough.

Once I got up on Astral I detected Death in the middle and Pestilence to
my right. Since I had good AC and the Orb, I opted for Death and headed
for the middle. Someone summoned lots of insects and I was able to dance
my way into the temple without Death ever getting adjancent to me.
Luckily enough, the temple belonged to Odin and after yet another
double-check I got some exercise for the choir.

Phew, that ended up being a long post. Hope at least someone enjoys it,
I sure did. :) The ending paste follows.

